      "content": "Amazon's AI was secretly penalizing women's resumes — and nobody caught it for years 🚨\n\nAmazon's AI was secretly penalizing women's resumes — and nobody caught it for years 🚨\n\nIn 2018, Amazon's internal AI screening tool was discovered to be systematically downgrading resumes that included words like 'women's' — as in 'women's chess club' or 'women's college.'\n\nWhy? It was trained on 10 years of Amazon's own hiring data — data reflecting a male-dominated tech industry.\n\nThe AI didn't have a bug. It learned the bias from humans.\n\nAmazon quietly shut it down without ever deploying it. But the lesson is still running in thousands of other systems.\n\n#aifacts #aibias #artificialintelligence #amazon #hiring #algorithmbias #machinelearning #techindustry",
