      "content": "AI catches 20% more cancers than doctors alone 🏥\n\nFDA-approved AI imaging tools now outperform solo radiologist reads by 20% in breast cancer detection.\n\nOver 700 AI medical devices have been FDA-cleared as of 2024.\n\nThis raises a legal question nobody wants to answer:\n\nIf AI-assisted diagnosis is provably more accurate — and your hospital doesn't use it — is that negligence?\n\nRadiology boards are already debating this. Malpractice insurers are watching.\n\nThe future isn't AI replacing doctors. It's AI making it legally risky NOT to use AI.\n\n#aifacts #medicalai #healthcare #fda #artificialintelligence #radiology #cancerdetection #futureofmedicine",
